// expect: exit 0
// env: AVIN_GC_STRESS=0
// Threads that end as fast as they are started, in rounds, so the workers hand back the stacks of
// ended threads while the main thread is still starting the next ones from those same stacks. The
// handles that keep a thread's storage and its stack alive count without atomics, so each is changed
// by one thread at a time: the starter lets go of its own before the new thread is ready, and a kept
// stack's count changes only under the spares' lock. Two hundred thousand threads in all.
import avin.threads.spawn

main() -> int
    var total = 0
    for round in 0..<20
        val threads = (0..<10000).map(i -> spawn(() -> i % 3 + round)).toVector
        for t in threads do total += t.join()
    println(total)
    var chained = 0
    for i in 0..<20000
        chained += spawn(() -> i % 5).join()
    println(chained)
    0
